ects. I could argue that B's reliability outweighs D's temperament concerns, especially given lack of reliability evidence for C and D. So I might change my vote to B.\n\nThus my public message: I note Emily's answer, that C lacks reliability evidence, which is a serious gap. I compare B's reliability (very conscientious) and D's responsibility but also temperament. I argue that B's reliability and stress handling make B the stronger candidate despite interpersonal concerns, which could be mitigated. So I shift my recommendation to Candidate B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote B."}
